        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "460ceb44-ad84-5fec-b12c-5f200aa69f3d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Spike Jonze\n- Bands: Weezer\n- Songs: \"Buddy Holly\", \"Undone – The Sweater Song\"\n- Albums: \"Weezer\" (\"The Blue Album\")\n- Charts: US Billboard 200\n\nFacts:\n- In 1994, Weezer released \"Buddy Holly\" as the second single from its debut album \"Weezer\" (\"The Blue Album\").\n- Weezer's debut album \"Weezer\" (\"The Blue Album\") was a huge commercial success and peaked at number 16 on the US Billboard 200.\n- Weezer's singles \"Undone – The Sweater Song\" and \"Buddy Holly\" helped launch the band into mainstream success.\n- Spike Jonze directed the music videos for \"Undone – The Sweater Song\" and \"Buddy Holly\", which aided Weezer's mainstream breakthrough.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d159116f-8403-5372-ab39-4f729a73609d",
        "text": "Page: Weezer discography. Sentence: The album was a huge commercial success, peaking at number 16 on the US \"Billboard\" 200 and spawning the singles \"Undone – The Sweater Song\" and \"Buddy Holly\", both of which were responsible for launching Weezer into mainstream success with the aid of music videos directed by Spike Jonze.\nPage: Buddy Holly (song). Sentence: It was released as the second single from the band's debut album \"Weezer\" (\"The Blue Album\") in 1994.",
